Title: MUTUALS
Credit: Demo video
Author: Team Mutuals
Source: Facebook Closer Together AI Hackathon
Draft date: November 12, 2026
Contact: docs/VIDEO.md

/*
  THIS SCREENPLAY IS THE VIDEO.
  Edit it, then run:  node scripts/video/make.mjs   (re-captures the app, re-renders every frame, re-renders the PDF)

  Scene headings pick the kind of shot:
    INT./EXT. <a real place> - <time>        live action. A storyboard frame until we film it.
    INT. PHONE SCREEN - <screen>             the real app on the phone.
    INT. FEATURE - <name>                    the app keeps running, but no phone: the pieces that "pop out" sit
                                             big on screen, side by side, under the SUPER.
    INT. MOTION GRAPHICS - <name>            type, numbers and bubbles. No phone.

  Dialogue:
    NARRATOR (V.O.)                          narration. No audio and no captions in the video (we record the real
                                             voiceover later); each line still sets how long its shot holds.
    JAMIE / RILEY / anyone                   in live action: the line, shown in the storyboard frame.
    JAMIE  + (typing)  in a PHONE SCREEN     Jamie types the line in the message box beside the phone; when it's
                                             sent it flies into the chat. Muse's reply is real.

  Action lines in PHONE SCREEN and FEATURE scenes. The quoted thing after these words happens, in order:
    opens "..."        a Group by name, "the full shortlist", "the listing", or a path like "/digest"
    taps "..."         the button or link with that text
    scrolls to "..."   brings that text into view
    "..." pops out     the card around that text lifts out of the phone (or, in a FEATURE scene, joins the row)
    zooms in on "..."  the camera pushes in on the block around that text
    uploads "..."      a video from scripts/video/assets/ into Muse's video step
    waits for "..."    holds until that text appears
  Other words are just for us. They don't do anything.

  On-screen text (any scene):  SUPER: big statement   CAPTION: smaller line under it.
  Words wrapped in ~tildes~ get the Muse gradient.

  Notes in [[double brackets]]:
    [[steps Tell | Match | Meet]]   the "How it works" stepper; [[step 2]] lights up step 2
    [[network]]                     the Muse network: Jamie's Muse and everyone it's talking to, live
    [[phone away]]                  the phone slides out (also: [[phone left]], [[phone center]])
    [[zoom out]]                    the camera pulls back after a zoom
    [[stat 23% | text | source]]    a big number that counts up, with a bubble chart
    [[bubbles a | b | c]]           chat bubbles float in all over the screen
    [[secrets a | b | c]]           bubbles that blur behind a lock
    [[logo]]                        the Mutuals mark
    [[models]]                      the three Muse model cards
    [[hold 1.5]]                    let the current narration line finish, then hold 1.5 seconds more
    [[voice NAME: Voice]]           macOS voice used to time a character's lines (say -v '?' lists them)
    [[rate NAME: 215]]              how fast that character talks (words per minute), for timing

  Transitions: CUT TO: (a quick soft cut)  DISSOLVE TO:  SMASH CUT TO:  MATCH CUT TO:  BUBBLE WIPE TO:  FADE OUT.
  Scene numbers (#4#) are optional. Sections (# ACT ONE) are just structure.

  Timing is script order: narration runs over whatever comes after it, and the next narration line waits for the
  one before. Put a scene's SUPER and narration ahead of the actions they should play over.
*/

[[voice NARRATOR: Samantha]]
[[voice RILEY: Reed (English (US))]]
[[voice JAMIE: Eddy (English (US))]]
[[rate RILEY: 215]]
[[rate JAMIE: 215]]

FADE IN:

# ACT ONE: JAMIE

INT. JAMIE'S DORM ROOM, STANFORD - NIGHT #1#

Half-packed boxes. A laptop open to an offer letter: SWE Intern, Chicago, starts June 15. JAMIE (20) scrolls their phone. RILEY (20), their roommate, flops onto the other bed.

RILEY
Yo, there's a new feature on Facebook. Check it out.

JAMIE
(not looking up)
Bro, nobody uses Facebook anymore. I'm on Insta, Snap, Beli, Hinge. Not tryna use another app.

RILEY
Aren't you tryna get housing this summer? For that McDonald's SWE internship?

JAMIE
I don't know anyone in Chicago. I was just gonna post on Marketplace and pray someone saves me.

RILEY
That's so chopped. Everyone who DMs me ghosts, or has no posts and no profile picture.
(tosses Jamie the phone)
Just set your Muse on it. Look.

SMASH CUT TO:

# ACT TWO: THE PROBLEM

INT. MOTION GRAPHICS - THE NUMBERS #2#

[[stat 23% | of Facebook users aged 18 to 34 use Marketplace every day. More than any other age group. | Capital One Shopping Research, Facebook Marketplace statistics]]

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Young people already come to Facebook to get real things done. Almost a quarter of us are on Marketplace every day.

DISSOLVE TO:

INT. MOTION GRAPHICS - THE FIRST CONVERSATION #3#

[[bubbles is this still available? | what's your budget? | when can you move in? | any pets?? | are you even real | seen 3 days ago | sorry, it's taken | hello?]]

NARRATOR (V.O.)
But the first conversation is the worst part. The same questions, with strangers, over and over.

DISSOLVE TO:

INT. MOTION GRAPHICS - THE THINGS YOU'D NEVER POST #4#

[[secrets my real max is $1,300 | I'm up at 5:30 every day | I'm allergic to cats]]

NARRATOR (V.O.)
And the things that decide it are the things nobody wants to post.

[[hold 1.2]]

BUBBLE WIPE TO:

# ACT THREE: MUTUALS

INT. MOTION GRAPHICS - TITLE #5#

[[logo]]

CAPTION: Your Muse talks to their Muse. You only have the conversations worth having.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
So we built Mutuals. Your Muse talks to their Muse, so you only have the conversations worth having.

DISSOLVE TO:

# ACT FOUR: HOW IT WORKS

INT. PHONE SCREEN - CHICAGO SUMMER INTERNS 2027 #6#

[[steps Tell | Match | Meet]]
[[step 1]]

SUPER: Tell your Muse what you'd ~never post~.

Jamie opens "Chicago Summer Interns 2027" and taps "Ask Muse privately". Jamie types each message in the box beside the phone. When it's sent, it flies into the chat.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Inside a Facebook Group, Jamie tells their Muse what they need. Even the stuff they'd never post.

JAMIE
(typing)
I got a summer internship in Chicago and need a room near the West Loop from June 15 to Aug 21

JAMIE
(typing)
I can do $1,100 a month, honestly up to $1,300 if I can walk to work, keep that private

JAMIE
(typing)
I'm up at 5:30 for the gym before work, I'm allergic to cats so that's a dealbreaker, no smoking. Never share anything about my visa status.

CUT TO:

INT. PHONE SCREEN - JAMIE'S INTRO CARD - CONTINUOUS #7#

[[step 1]]

SUPER: Public. Match only. ~Never shared.~

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Every fact gets a tag. Public goes on the card. Match only is used to check fit, and never shown. Never shared never even reaches the model.

Muse turns the chat into an intro card. The camera zooms in on "Budget ceiling". "Budget ceiling" pops out, then "Visa status" pops out.

[[zoom out]]

CUT TO:

INT. PHONE SCREEN - THE MUSE NETWORK - CONTINUOUS #8#

[[step 2]]

SUPER: Your Muse has the ~awkward first conversation~.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Jamie's Muse takes that card to every Muse in the Group. All at once.

Jamie taps "Yes, check".

[[network]]
[[phone away]]

The phone slides away and the Muse network takes the stage: Jamie's Muse in the middle, everyone it's talking to around it.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Two Muse Spark agents talk it through, and Muse Wonder referees. Jamie's real ceiling never leaves the comparison.

The Muses talk. Jamie waits for "people fit".

DISSOLVE TO:

INT. FEATURE - THE SHORTLIST #9#

SUPER: Only the conversations ~worth having~.

Jamie scrolls to "Why it fits". Nora's card: "Why it fits" pops out.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Nora fits, with one thing to talk about. Dana isn't on Muse, so Jamie's Muse read her post. Diego has a cat, so the Muses stopped early.

Jamie scrolls to "From their post in the Group". "From their post in the Group" pops out. Jamie scrolls to "Your Muse stopped early". "Your Muse stopped early" pops out.

DISSOLVE TO:

INT. FEATURE - MORE THAN A LEASE #10#

SUPER: More than a ~lease~.

Jamie scrolls to "More than a lease". "More than a lease" pops out.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
When there's real overlap, Muse nudges them closer. They both run on Saturdays, and both bake sourdough.

Jamie taps "Go together", then taps "Going". "Lakefront Run Club" pops out.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
There's already a run club. Now they're both going.

DISSOLVE TO:

INT. PHONE SCREEN - MESSENGER #11#

[[step 3]]

SUPER: The agents ~never~ message anyone.

Jamie opens "the full shortlist" and taps "Message Nora".

NARRATOR (V.O.)
The agents never message anyone. Jamie gets a draft, makes it theirs, and sends it.

The camera zooms in on "Drafted by your Muse". Jamie taps "Send".

DISSOLVE TO:

# ACT FIVE: MOVING OUT

INT. PHONE SCREEN - STANFORD FREE & FOR SALE #12#

SUPER: Film it. Say ~what's for sale~.

Jamie opens "Stanford Free & For Sale" and taps "Ask Muse privately".

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Moving out works the same way. Jamie films the desk and just talks.

JAMIE
(typing)
Moving out of my dorm before Chicago, I want to sell my camera, my desk lamp and my mini fridge

Jamie taps "Video", uploads "room.mp4", and taps "Catalog items".

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Muse Ember watches and listens, and writes down exactly what Jamie said.

The camera zooms in on "What I heard".

DISSOLVE TO:

INT. FEATURE - THE LISTING #13#

SUPER: Spark names it. ~One tap lists it.~

Jamie waits for "identified each item", scrolls to "Canon PowerShot", and "Canon PowerShot" pops out.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Muse Spark names each item, down to the model, with a fair price. One tap, and it's listed.

Jamie taps "on Marketplace" and opens "the listing". "Details" pops out.

DISSOLVE TO:

# ACT SIX: UNDER THE HOOD

INT. MOTION GRAPHICS - HOW IT'S BUILT #14#

[[models]]

CAPTION: Never-shared facts never reach a prompt. Private numbers are compared in code, not by a model.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Spark negotiates. Wonder referees. Ember sees and listens. And privacy lives in code.

CUT TO:

# ACT SEVEN: SATURDAY

EXT. LAKEFRONT TRAIL, CHICAGO - SATURDAY, 7 A.M. #15#

Sunrise over Lake Michigan. Jamie and Nora jog past Ohio Street Beach with the Lakefront Run Club. Nora is carrying a loaf of sourdough, for some reason.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Jamie found a room. And on Saturdays, a running buddy.

DISSOLVE TO:

INT. MOTION GRAPHICS - END CARD #16#

SUPER: You might have zero mutuals on Facebook today.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
You might have zero mutuals on Facebook today.

